function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    var page := dval({source_page: ""})
    page["source_page"] = "capy-04-expressions-and-control-flow"
    page["kind"] = "guide"
    page["slug"] = "expressions-and-control-flow"
    page["route"] = "/doc/guide/expressions-and-control-flow/"
    page["title"] = "4. Expressions and control flow"
    page["content"] = "An expression produces a value or performs an action. Capy evaluates listed expressions from left to right.\n\n## Calculate a value\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var price := 6\n    var quantity := 2\n    var total := price * quantity\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n12\n\n```\n\n`*` runs before `+` and `-`. Parentheses make the intended order explicit.\n\n## Declare and assign locals\n\n`:=` declares a local and infers its type. `=` replaces its value:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var count := 1\n    count = count + 1\n    print(count, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA local exists until the end of its block. An inner block can declare a new local with the same name without changing the outer local.\n\n## Conditions\n\nUse `if` to select code:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := 12\n    if total > 10 {\n        print(\"large\\n\")\n    } else {\n        print(\"small\\n\")\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n\nCapy evaluates each condition as `bool(condition)`. A condition can use any value with a `bool` constructor.\n\nString conditions use boolean-word parsing, not truthiness. `\"true\"`, `\"1\"`, and `\"yes\"` produce true. `\"hello\"`, `\"0\"`, and `\"\"` produce false. `&&` and `||` stop as soon as the result is known.\n\nAn `if` with `else` can also produce a value:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := 12\n    var label := if total > 10 {\n        -> \"large\"\n    } else {\n        -> \"small\"\n    }\n    print(label, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nEach reachable branch that produces a value must produce the same type. A branch that returns or traps does not produce a value.\n\n## Loops\n\nA `while` loop repeats while its condition is true:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var index := 0\n    while index < 3 {\n        print(index, \"\\n\")\n        index = index + 1"
    page["content"] = string(page["content"], "") + "\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA `for` loop reads a half-open `s32` range, an array, or a `dval` map or list:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    for number := 1..4 {\n        print(number, \"\\n\")\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThe range is half-open. `1..4` contains `1`, `2`, and `3`. A range permits one loop value only.\n\nOptional metadata follows the value:\n\n```capy\nfunction show(names : [string], profile : dval) {\n    for name, index := names { print(index, \": \", name, \"\\n\") }\n    for item, key := profile { print(key, \": \", item, \"\\n\") }\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    show([\"Ada\"], {role: \"admin\"})\n}\n\n```\n\n\nAn array index has type `s32`. A `dval` key has type `string`. `dval` list keys are decimal strings. Structs are not iterable. The old `=` and `in` forms are invalid.\n\nArray and `dval` loops recheck the current count before each iteration. A loop can visit items added while it runs. Shrinkage cannot cause an invalid access. `dval` loop items are copies. An array loop retains its current managed item while the body runs.\n\nUse `break` to leave the nearest loop. Use `continue` to start its next iteration.\n\n## Blocks\n\nA block yields a value when its final reachable item starts with `->`:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := {\n        var subtotal := 10\n        -> subtotal + 2\n    }\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThis makes `total` equal to `12`. A block can keep temporary locals close to the calculation that uses them.\n"
    page["label"] = "4. Expressions and control flow"
    page["capy_sig_lines"] = dval([])
    page["param_lines"] = dval([])
    page["notes"] = dval([])
    page["warnings"] = dval([])
    page["see"] = dval([{label: "3. Types", href: "/doc/guide/values-and-types/"}, {label: "5. Functions", href: "/doc/guide/functions-and-closures/"}, {label: "7. Arrays, tuples, and structs", href: "/doc/guide/collections-and-records/"}])
    page["examples"] = dval([])
    page["guide_examples"] = dval([{entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var price := 6\n    var quantity := 2\n    var total := price * quantity\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n", output: "12\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var count := 1\n    count = count + 1\n    print(count, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := 12\n    if total > 10 {\n        print(\"large\\n\")\n    } else {\n        print(\"small\\n\")\n    }\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := 12\n    var label := if total > 10 {\n        -> \"large\"\n    } else {\n        -> \"small\"\n    }\n    print(label, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var index := 0\n    while index < 3 {\n        print(index, \"\\n\")\n        index = index + 1\n    }\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    for number := 1..4 {\n        print(number, \"\\n\")\n    }\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function show(names : [string], profile : dval) {\n    for name, index := names { print(index, \": \", name, \"\\n\") }\n    for item, key := profile { print(key, \": \", item, \"\\n\") }\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    show([\"Ada\"], {role: \"admin\"})\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total := {\n        var subtotal := 10\n        -> subtotal + 2\n    }\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}])
    component_render("/doc/components/doc_page.capy", page)
}
